  "subtitle": "A 2-axis joystick as a plane of sound, not a list of patches",
  "blurb": "The Prophet VS was the first commercially shipped 'vector synthesizer.' Its one defining control is a joystick whose x and y axes continuously crossfade and mix four digital waveforms across a two-dimensional plane of timbre. Instead of dialing through a menu of sounds, the performer steers a cursor across a map of sound — a genuinely odd, embodied input model.",
